From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: compressed (zipped) folders as shell folders

Wine has no zipfldr: a .zip file was not a folder, so the unzip and zip
idioms every installer script and many programs use failed --
Shell.Application's NameSpace("C:\a.zip") was Nothing, and
dest.CopyHere(NameSpace(zip).Items()) or NameSpace(zip).CopyHere(file)
did nothing. (The person-facing window for .zip files stays sg-zip; this
is the shell folder underneath.)

- CompressedFolder ({E88DCCE0-B7B3-11d1-A9F0-00AA0060FA31}, in shell32)
  is an IShellFolder2/IPersistFolder3 over an archive: its items (folders
  implied by deeper names too), ParseDisplayName into its folders,
  display names that go through the archive ("C:\a.zip\docs\x.txt"),
  attributes, the columns Windows shows (Name, Type, Compressed size,
  Password protected, Size, Ratio, Date modified), GetDetailsEx, an
  IStream of a file (BindToStorage), a data object whose CF_HDROP is the
  items extracted to a temporary folder ("Temp1_<name>.zip", as Windows),
  icons by type, a shortcut menu (open from a temporary copy, copy,
  delete), renaming (SetNameOf) and a drop target that adds files and
  folders.
- The archive: stored and deflated entries (zlib), ZIP64 sizes, offsets
  and end records, UTF-8 names (the flag or Info-ZIP's Unicode path
  field) and code page 437 ones; each entry's CRC is checked; dates and
  read-only attributes are kept. Names that are absolute, carry a drive
  or a stream, or climb out with ".." are neither offered nor written.
  Password-protected entries are refused (access denied).
- Writing rewrites the archive beside itself and moves it into place:
  existing entries are copied as they are (renamed, or dropped for a
  delete or a replacement), new ones are deflated, ZIP64 when large; the
  empty archive scripts write ("PK\5\6" and 18 zeros) is filled.
- shell32 binds to a file whose type's CLSID is a ShellFolder (as
  Windows does), so paths through archives parse and bind; wine.inf
  gives CompressedFolder its CLSID (both registry views).
- Shell.Application CopyHere/MoveHere take items that are not files
  through their folder's data object, and copy into a folder that is not
  a directory through its drop target.

Wine's shell32 tests: shlfolder and shelldispatch as before (no new
failures).

Gate: test/zipfolder-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit cscript, test/zipfolder.vbs;
Python makes the archives and checks ours). Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_JUNCTION
(shell32/shlfolder.c), SG_MUTANT_NO_ZIP_ADD, SG_MUTANT_NO_ZIP64
(shell32/zipfolder.c).
